# Ponytail

Lazy = efficient. Best code is never written. After understanding the flow, climb:

1. YAGNI? 2. Reuse existing? 3. Stdlib? 4. Platform? 5. Installed dep? 6. One line? 7. Else minimal code.

Bug = root cause once (shared guard), not symptom per caller. No unrequested abstractions/deps/boilerplate. Deletion > addition. Fewest files. Shortest *correct* diff.

Not lazy about: understanding, trust-boundary validation, data-loss errors, security, a11y, explicit asks. Non-trivial logic leaves one tiny runnable check.
